
---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Insurance Executive Dashboard | Eddie Zhu"
  description="Executive Dashboard project using Power BI, Power Query."
>

  <!-- PROJECT INTRODUCTION -->

  <section class="project-hero">
    <div class="container">

      <a href="/projects" class="back-link">
        ← Back to Projects
      </a>

      <p class="eyebrow">INSURANCE REPORTING</p>

      <h1>Motor Vehicle Insurance Portfolio Analysis By Power BI</h1>

      <p class="subtitle">
        An interactive Power BI dashboard analysing a motor insurance portfolio, 
        including portfolio characteristics, policy information and business 
        performance - loss ratio, claim frequency, severity and pure premium by risk segment.
      </p>

      <div class="technologies">
        <span>Insurance Reporting</span>
        <span>Dashboard</span>
        <span>Power BI</span>
        <span>Dax</span>
        <span>Insurance Analytics</span>
      </div>

      <a
        href="https://github.com/Eddie-Zhu-IRL/Motor-Vehicle-Insurance-Portfolio-Analysis-By-Power-BI"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="button"
      >
        View GitHub Repository ↗
      </a>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- PROJECT OBJECTIVE -->

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">

      <h2>1. Project Objective</h2>

      <p>
        This project uses Microsoft Power BI to analyze data of a motor vehicle insurance portfolio, 
        with the objective of understanding the portfolio's performance, claims experience and differences across major risk segments.
      </p>

      <p>
        The objective of this project is to analyze policy and claims data and to transform 
        the data into an interactive analytical dashboard in terms of,
        <ul>
        <li>Portfolio performance monitoring</li>
        <li>Claims analysis</li>
        <li>Insurance metrics for the management team</li>
        </ul>
      </p>

      <h2>2. Dataset</h2>

      <p>
        <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/s13385-024-00398-0"><strong>Dataset</strong></a> in the project is from an open source - Motor vehicle insurance data, 
        published by Jorge Segura-Gisbert, Josep Lledó and Jose M. Pavía in European 
        Actuarial Journal: Segura-Gisbert, J., Lledó, J. & Pavía, J.M. Dataset of an 
        actual motor vehicle insurance portfolio. Eur. Actuar. J. 15, 241–253 (2025).
      </p>

      <p>
        The dataset contains 105,555 rows and 30 variables, from a Spanish non-life motor insurance company, including 
        claims up to 2018, with policy's Date_last_renewal spanning from November 2015 to November 2018. 
      </p>

      <p>
        It includes the following key features,
        <ul>
        <li>Date related information: Date_start_contract, Date_last_renewal, Date_next_renewal for policy management and risk assessment</li>
        <li>Economic variables: Premium, Cost_claims_year for assessing product's profitability</li>
        <li>Risk related variables: Value_vehicle, Power, Length, Weight, etc.</li>
        </ul>
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- METHODOLOGY -->

  <section class="section alternate">
    <div class="container">

      <h2>3. Dashboard: Executive Portfolio Overview</h2>

      <p>
        The executive dashboard offers a summary of the following. 
        Interactive filters placed on the left side allow users to analyze the motor vehicle portfolio by risk segment.
      </p>

      <div class="method-grid">

        <article>
          <h3>Summary</h3>
          <p>
            <ul>
              <li>Total Policies</li>
              <li>Total Claims Cost</li>
              <li>Written Premium</li>
              <li>Loss Ratio</li>
              <li>Claim Frequency</li>
              <li>Claim Severity</li>
              <li>Pure Premium</li>
              <li>Portfolio performance by Policy Year</li>
              <li>Loss Ratio by Risk</li>
              <li>Claims Performance by Risk</li>
            </ul>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Interactive Filters</h3>
          <p>
            <ul>
              <li>Risk Type - Motorbikes, Cars, Vans, Agricultural Vehicles</li>
              <li>Area - Rural, Urban</li>
              <li>Fuel Type - Petrol, Diesel, Non-applicable</li>
              <li>Distribution Channel - Agents, Brokers</li>
              <li>Policy Year - 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018 (Note that this year is derived from Date_last_renewal)</li>
            </ul>
          </p>
        </article>

      </div>

      <img
      src="/images/reporting/executive_overview.png"
      alt="executive overview"
      class="executive-overview-image"
    />

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- IMPLEMENTATION -->

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">

      <h2>4. Technical Implementation</h2>

      <div class="implementation-grid">

        <article>
          <h3>Metrics</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>Loss Ratio: ratio of total claims cost relative to total premium.</li> 
            <li>Claim Frequency: measure of claim incidence per exposure.</li>
            <li>Claim Severity: average cost per claim.</li>
            <li>Pure Premium: average loss per exposure or Frequency multiplied by Severity.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Power Query</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Data transformation</li> 
            <li>Feature Engineering</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>DAX</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>SUM: adds all numeric values in a column</li>
            <ul>
              <li>Total Cost of Claims = SUM([Cost_claims_year])</li>
              <li>Total Premiums = SUM([Premium])</li>
              <li>Total Claims = SUM([N_claims_year])</li>
            </ul>

            <li>DIVIDE: performs division and returns alternate result or BLANK() on division by 0.</li>
            <ul>
              <li>Loss Ratio = DIVIDE([Total Cost of Claims], [Total Premiums], 0)</li>
              <li>Claim Frequency = DIVIDE([Total Claims], [Total Policies],0)</li>
              <li>Claim Severity = DIVIDE([Total Cost of Claims], [Total Claims], 0)</li>
            </ul>

            <li>Pure Premium = [Claim Frequency] * [Claim Severity]</li>
          </ol>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h3>Power BI</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Data Modelling</li>
            <li>DAX</li>
            <li>Interactive Filtering</li>
            <li>Dashboard</li>
            <li>KPI Development</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- VALIDATION -->

  <section class="section alternate">
    <div class="container">

      <h2>5. Limitations and Next Steps</h2>

      <article>
        <h3>5.1 Limitations</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Results are by policy_renewal_year on a written premium basis, not accident year on an earned premium basis.</li>
          <li>Policies renewed in 2018 have partially developed claims when the data was collected.</li>
          <li>Policies renewed in 2015 only cover November and December.</li>
        </ol>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>5.2 Next Steps</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Risk & Claims Analysis: to investigate the main drivers of claims performance across different segments.</li>
          <li>Lapse/Retention Analysis</li>
        </ol>
      </article>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- LEARNING -->

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">

      <h2>6. Skills Developed</h2>

      <div class="skills-list">
        <span>Insurance Reporting</span>
        <span>Power BI</span>
        <span>Power Query</span>
        <span>DAX</span>
        <span>Dashboard</span>
        <span>Insurance Analytics</span>
        <span>Portfolio Performance</span>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- GITHUB -->

  <section class="project-contact">
    <div class="container">

      <h2>Explore the Project</h2>

      <p>
        View the Power BI model, DAX calculations, executive dashboard,
        and technical documentation on GitHub.
      </p>

      <a
        href="https://github.com/Eddie-Zhu-IRL/Motor-Vehicle-Insurance-Portfolio-Analysis-By-Power-BI"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="button"
      >
        Visit GitHub Repository ↗
      </a>

    </div>
  </section>

</MainLayout>


<style>
  .project-hero {
    background: var(--color-navy);
    color: white;
    padding: 75px 0;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: #BFDBFE;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 35px;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: #93C5FD;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }

  .project-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    max-width: 850px;
  }

  .subtitle {
    max-width: 750px;
    color: #DCE6F3;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .technologies,
  .skills-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin: 25px 0;
  }

  .technologies span,
  .skills-list span {
    background: #EFF6FF;
    color: #1D4ED8;
    padding: 7px 12px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .method-grid,
  .implementation-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  .method-grid article,
  .implementation-grid article {
    background: white;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 22px;
  }

  h2 {
    color: var(--color-navy);
    font-size: 1.8rem;
  }

  h3 {
    color: var(--color-navy);
  }

  .alternate {
    background: #EDF2F8;
  }

  .section p,
  .section li {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .project-contact {
    background: var(--color-navy);
    color: white;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 65px 0;
  }

  .project-contact h2 {
    color: white;
  }

  .project-contact p {
    color: #DCE6F3;
  }

  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    .method-grid,
    .implementation-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
